---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title={"Auspicious Music — Independent music production guides"}
  description={"An independent publication for music production, Ableton, recording, sound design, and music for media."}
  canonicalPath={"/"}
  lang={"en"}
  noindex={false}
  loadStringField={true}
>
<Fragment slot="head">
<style is:global>
@layer components {

  /* ══ Hero ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     Revision 4 — the masthead is the type, and the string is playable.

     Earlier passes leaned on photography: first a framed object, then a
     full-bleed band, then a portrait. Each put the argument in a picture.
     This one puts it in the typography and gives the reader one thing to
     do — a taut string across the headline that answers the pointer and
     rings down on its own physics.

     That is not ornament. The brand mark is a driving wave and its damped
     response; this is the same idea made operable, on a publication about
     how sound behaves. It is also the only motion above the fold, it
     never loops, and it stops dead once the string is at rest.          */
  /* Full-viewport masthead. svh rather than vh so a mobile browser's
     collapsing address bar cannot push the footer row out of frame.
     min-block-size, not height: on a short laptop window the scene grows
     with its contents instead of clipping them. */
  .hero {
    background: var(--canvas);
    color: var(--ink);
    position: relative;
    overflow: clip;
    min-block-size: calc(100svh - var(--header-h));
    display: flex;
  }
  .hero > .shell {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;                /* type sits above the string field */
    inline-size: 100%;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-rows: auto 1fr auto auto;
    padding-block: clamp(1.25rem, 2.5vh, 2rem) 0;
  }

  .hero__note {
    margin-left: auto;
    max-width: 34ch;
    font-size: var(--t-ui-sm);
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  @media (min-width: 860px) { .hero__note { text-align: right; } }

  /* The stage holds the headline and the string on the same layer, so the
     string crosses the letterforms rather than sitting under them. It
     takes the free row and centres within it. */
  /* Weighted to the bottom of the free row, so the open space collects
     above the headline rather than splitting either side of it. */
  .hero__stage {
    display: grid;
    align-content: end;
    padding-block: clamp(2rem, 6vh, 5rem) clamp(1.5rem, 3vh, 2.5rem);
  }
  /* On a phone the headline is only two short lines, so bottom-weighting
     the free row leaves a dead field above it. Centred instead, the space
     splits and the scene reads as composed rather than bottom-heavy. */
  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .hero__stage { align-content: center; padding-block: clamp(1rem, 3vh, 2rem); }
  }

  /* Two long lines rather than three uneven ones: "Make" on its own left a
     third of the measure empty. Set at a size where the second line very
     nearly spans the container, which is what gives the block its weight. */
  .hero__title {
    font-size: clamp(2.75rem, 0.5rem + 11.4vw, 10.5rem);   /* 44 → 168 */
    line-height: 0.85;
    letter-spacing: -0.048em;
    font-weight: 600;
    text-wrap: nowrap;
  }
  .hero__title span { display: block; }
  .hero__title span:nth-child(2) { margin-left: 9%; }
  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .hero__title span:nth-child(2) { margin-left: 5%; }
  }
  /* Short windows: a 168px headline plus the footer rows does not fit a
     600px-tall viewport, so the display scale gives way rather than the
     scene overflowing. */
  @media (min-width: 900px) and (max-height: 760px) {
    .hero__title { font-size: clamp(2.75rem, 0.5rem + 7.4vw, 6.75rem); }
    .hero__string { block-size: 170px; }
  }

  /* The string field occupies the whole masthead rather than a single
     band. Six strings distributed across the upper two thirds — which is
     precisely the region that was previously empty. Transparent to clicks
     so the type, the actions and the selection behaviour underneath are
     untouched; the pointer is read from .hero itself. */
  .hero__string {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    inline-size: 100%;
    block-size: 100%;
    pointer-events: none;
    z-index: 0;
  }

  /* Scroll cue — replaces the Latest row. A masthead at full viewport
     height needs to say that something follows; it does not need to
     advertise an article to do it. */
  .hero__scroll {
    position: relative;
    padding-block: 1rem clamp(1.25rem, 2.5vh, 1.75rem);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .hero__scroll::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute; top: -4px; left: 0;
    inline-size: 7px; block-size: 7px; border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--ember-bright);
  }
  .hero__scroll span {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--t-meta);
    letter-spacing: var(--tr-caps);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .hero__foot {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1.25rem 2rem;
    padding-bottom: clamp(1.5rem, 3vh, 2.25rem);
  }
  .hero__actions { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.75rem; }

  .hero__hint {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--t-meta);
    letter-spacing: var(--tr-caps);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--muted);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .hero__hint button {
    font: inherit;
    letter-spacing: inherit;
    text-transform: inherit;
    color: var(--ink);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line-strong);
    padding-bottom: 1px;
    transition: border-color var(--dur-fast) var(--ease);
  }
  .hero__hint button:hover { border-bottom-color: var(--ink); }


  .line-mask { display: block; overflow: hidden; padding-bottom: 0.06em; }
  .line-mask > span { display: block; }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {
    .line-mask > span { animation: line-in 620ms var(--ease-out) both; }
    .line-mask:nth-of-type(2) > span { animation-delay: 80ms; }
  }
  @keyframes line-in { from { transform: translateY(102%); } }

  /* ══ 2 · topic portals ══════════════════════════════════════════════ */
  .portal { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .portals > li:last-child { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .portal a {
    display: grid; gap: 0.5rem 2.5rem;
    padding-block: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 2.5rem);
    text-decoration: none; align-items: baseline;
    transition: background-color var(--dur-fast) var(--ease);
  }
  .portal a:hover { background: var(--surface); }
  .portal__n {
    font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: var(--t-meta);
    color: var(--muted); letter-spacing: var(--tr-meta);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }
  .portal h3 { font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 1.2rem + 2.1vw, 3rem); letter-spacing: -0.021em; }
  .portal p { color: var(--muted); font-size: 1.0625rem; line-height: 1.6; max-width: 52ch; }
  .portal__go { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.4375rem; font-size: var(--t-ui-sm); font-weight: 550; }
  .portal a:hover .portal__go { gap: 0.6875rem; }
  .portal__go svg { width: 14px; height: 14px; }
  @media (min-width: 900px) {
    .portal a { grid-template-columns: 3.5rem minmax(0, 15rem) minmax(0, 1fr) auto; align-items: start; }
    .portal__n, .portal__go { padding-top: 0.65rem; }
  }

  /* ══ 3 · start here ═════════════════════════════════════════════════ */
  .start { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); gap: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4rem); }
  @media (min-width: 1000px) { .start { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.15fr) minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 4.5rem; } }
  .start__lead h3 { font-size: clamp(1.625rem, 1.15rem + 1.7vw, 2.375rem); letter-spacing: -0.019em; margin-top: 1.25rem; }
  .start__lead p { color: var(--ink-soft); margin-top: 0.875rem; font-size: 1.0625rem; line-height: 1.6; max-width: 48ch; }
  .start__lead .meta { margin-top: 1.25rem; }
  .start__lead a { text-decoration: none; display: block; }
  .start__lead a:hover h3 { text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 4px; text-decoration-thickness: 1px; }
  .start__lead .ph { aspect-ratio: 16 / 10; }

  .numbered li { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .numbered li:last-child { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .numbered a {
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: 2.25rem minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 0.375rem 1rem; padding-block: 1.375rem; text-decoration: none;
    transition: background-color var(--dur-fast) var(--ease);
  }
  .numbered a:hover { background: var(--surface); }
  .numbered__n {
    font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: var(--t-meta);
    color: var(--muted); padding-top: 0.28rem; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }
  .numbered h4 { font-size: 1.125rem; letter-spacing: -0.012em; }
  .numbered .meta { grid-column: 2; margin-top: 0.375rem; }

  /* ══ 4 · featured lab ═══════════════════════════════════════════════ */
  .lab__inner { display: grid; gap: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4rem); align-items: center; }
  @media (min-width: 1000px) { .lab__inner { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.25fr) minmax(0, 1fr); } }
  .lab h2 { font-size: clamp(2rem, 1.15rem + 2.6vw, 3.25rem); max-width: 18ch; }
  .lab p { color: var(--dark-muted); margin-top: 1.25rem; max-width: 46ch; font-size: 1.0625rem; line-height: 1.65; }
  .lab .meta { margin-top: 1.75rem; }
  .lab .link { margin-top: 2rem; }
  .lab__art { border-radius: var(--r-media); overflow: hidden; background: var(--dark-surface); }
  .lab__art img {
    inline-size: 100%;
    aspect-ratio: 5 / 4;
    object-fit: cover;
    object-position: 55% 62%;
  }

  /* ══ 5 · tools ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     Deliberately the densest block on the page. A calculator row should
     look like something you use, not something you are sold.          */
  .tools-band { background: var(--surface); }
  .tool-row { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .tools-list > li:last-child { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .tool-row a {
    display: grid; gap: 0.5rem 2.5rem; padding-block: 1.5rem;
    text-decoration: none; align-items: baseline;
    transition: background-color var(--dur-fast) var(--ease);
  }
  .tool-row a:hover { background: var(--surface-bright); }
  .tool-row h3 { font-size: 1.375rem; letter-spacing: -0.015em; }
  .tool-row p { color: var(--muted); font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.55; max-width: 56ch; }
  .tool-row__io {
    font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: var(--t-meta);
    letter-spacing: var(--tr-meta); color: var(--ink-soft);
    white-space: nowrap; overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis;
  }
  @media (min-width: 900px) {
    .tool-row a { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 16rem) minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 11rem); align-items: start; }
    .tool-row__io { text-align: right; padding-top: 0.3rem; }
  }

  /* ══ 6 · archive ════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */
  .record { border-top: 1px solid var(--line-strong); padding-block: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem); }
  .record:last-of-type { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line-strong); }
  .record__grid { display: grid; gap: 1.25rem 3rem; }
  @media (min-width: 900px) { .record__grid { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 18rem) minmax(0, 1fr); } }
  .record h3 { font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 1.15rem + 1.1vw, 2rem); letter-spacing: -0.017em; margin-top: 0.625rem; }
  .record p { color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 1.0625rem; line-height: 1.65; max-width: 60ch; }
  .record__facts { display: grid; gap: 0.625rem; margin-top: 1.5rem; }
  .record .link { margin-top: 1.5rem; }
  .fact {
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: 8.5rem minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 0.75rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: var(--t-meta);
    letter-spacing: var(--tr-meta); padding-block: 0.5rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .fact dt { color: var(--muted); }
  .fact dd { color: var(--ink-soft); }
  @media (max-width: 560px) { .fact { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 0.1875rem; } }

  /* ══ 7 · acoustic story ═════════════════════════════════════════════ */
  .story__media { position: relative; border-radius: var(--r-media); overflow: hidden; }
  .story__media img { aspect-ratio: 16 / 9; object-fit: cover; }
  .story__body { display: grid; gap: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 2.5rem); margin-top: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem); }
  @media (min-width: 900px) { .story__body { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 4rem; } }
  .story h2 { max-width: 16ch; }
  .story p { color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 1.0625rem; line-height: 1.7; max-width: 56ch; }
  .story__links { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.75rem 1.5rem; margin-top: 1.75rem; }
}
</style>
</Fragment>

<main id="content">

  <!-- 1 ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── hero -->
  <section class="hero" data-od-id="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
    <canvas class="hero__string" data-string aria-hidden="true"></canvas>

    <div class="shell">

      <p class="hero__note">
        Practical, source-labelled guides for music production, Ableton, recording,
        sound design and music for media. Each page tells you what was tested, researched or preserved.
      </p>

      <div class="hero__stage">
        <h1 id="hero-title" class="hero__title">
          <span>Make sound</span>
          <span>with intent.</span>
        </h1>
      </div>

      <div class="hero__foot">
        <div class="hero__actions">
          <a class="btn btn--primary" href="/ableton/">Explore the guides</a>
          <a class="btn btn--quiet" href="/download/">Browse legacy resources</a>
        </div>
        <p class="hero__hint">
          <button type="button" data-string-pluck>Play the strings</button> — drag one and the others answer.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="hero__scroll" aria-hidden="true">
        <span>Scroll</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 2 · topic portals -->
  <section class="band band--tight" aria-labelledby="portals-title">
    <div class="shell" style="position:relative">
      <span class="rail" data-rail style="left:calc(var(--gutter) * -0.55)" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <h2 id="portals-title" style="position:absolute;width:1px;height:1px;overflow:hidden;clip-path:inset(50%)">Where to start by topic</h2>
      <ul class="portals" data-reveal-group>
        <li class="portal" data-reveal><a href="/ableton/"><span class="portal__n">01</span><h3>Ableton</h3><p>File management, Sampler and controller systems grounded in official behavior — with test limits stated where hardware experience is missing.</p><span class="portal__go">Open hub →</span></a></li>
        <li class="portal" data-reveal><a href="/recording/"><span class="portal__n">02</span><h3>Recording</h3><p>Repeatable room and microphone decisions for acoustic instruments, beginning with viola and domestic spaces.</p><span class="portal__go">Open hub →</span></a></li>
        <li class="portal" data-reveal><a href="/sound-design/"><span class="portal__n">03</span><h3>Sound Design</h3><p>Sampling workflows that keep source recordings, edits and mappings understandable instead of hiding them behind a preset.</p><span class="portal__go">Open hub →</span></a></li>
        <li class="portal" data-reveal><a href="/music-for-media/"><span class="portal__n">04</span><h3>Music for Media</h3><p>Briefing, rights and live-performance planning for films, ceremonies and projects governed by a larger timeline.</p><span class="portal__go">Open hub →</span></a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 3 · start here -->
  <section class="band" aria-labelledby="start-title">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-head"><h2 id="start-title">Start with the work in front of you</h2><p>Eight published guides. Each one starts with a real task and shows its method, sources and limits.</p></div>
      <div class="start">
        <article class="start__lead" data-reveal>
          <a href="/music-production/ableton-project-handoff/">
            <div class="ph" aria-hidden="true"><span class="ph__label"><strong>Project map</strong><br>Set · collected media · dependency note · reference mix · stems</span></div>
            <h3>An Ableton project handoff another computer can actually open</h3>
            <p>Collect media, expose plug-in dependencies, print safety stems and make the next decision obvious.</p>
            <p class="meta"><span>Music Production</span><span>8 min</span><span>Source-based guide</span></p>
          </a>
        </article>
        <ol class="numbered" data-reveal-group>
          <li data-reveal><a href="/recording/acoustic-instruments/viola-microphone-placement/"><span class="numbered__n">01</span><h4>Viola microphone placement: three useful starting positions</h4><p class="meta"><span>Recording</span><span>9 min</span></p></a></li>
          <li data-reveal><a href="/sound-design/when-to-record-strings-instead-of-using-a-library/"><span class="numbered__n">02</span><h4>When to record a string part instead of using a library</h4><p class="meta"><span>Sound Design</span><span>8 min</span></p></a></li>
          <li data-reveal><a href="/music-for-media/music-clearance-for-small-film-projects/"><span class="numbered__n">03</span><h4>Music clearance for a small film before edit lock</h4><p class="meta"><span>Music for Media</span><span>8 min</span></p></a></li>
          <li data-reveal><a href="/music-for-media/planning-live-viola-for-a-wedding-ceremony/"><span class="numbered__n">04</span><h4>Planning live viola for a wedding ceremony</h4><p class="meta"><span>Events</span><span>7 min</span></p></a></li>
          <li data-reveal><a href="/ableton/midi-fighter-twister-review/"><span class="numbered__n">05</span><h4>Design a controller mapping before the knobs</h4><p class="meta"><span>Ableton</span><span>8 min</span></p></a></li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 4 · featured method -->
  <section class="band band--wide band-dark lab" aria-labelledby="lab-title">
    <div class="shell lab__inner">
      <figure class="lab__art" data-reveal><img src="/assets/hero-portrait.png" width="928" height="1152" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Abstract editorial image of a metal block and a tensioned string."><figcaption class="kicker" style="padding:1rem">Editorial illustration — not a test photograph</figcaption></figure>
      <div data-reveal data-reveal-delay="120"><p class="kicker">Method guide</p><h2 id="lab-title" style="margin-top:.875rem">Build a small sampled instrument without losing the source</h2><p>Define the range, keep source and edits separate, map one dimension at a time and package the Project so the samples travel with it. The workflow is designed to be repeated with recordings you own.</p><p class="meta"><span>Ableton Live 12 documentation</span><span>Sampler</span><span>10 min</span></p><a class="link" href="/sound-design/sampled-instruments/building-a-sampled-instrument/">Read the workflow →</a></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 5 · tools -->
  <section class="band tools-band" aria-labelledby="tools-title">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-head"><h2 id="tools-title">Small tools, local answers</h2><p>No account, tracking or server round-trip. These calculators run in the browser.</p></div>
      <ul class="tools-list" data-reveal-group>
        <li class="tool-row" data-reveal><a href="/resources/tools/delay-and-reverb/"><h3>Delay &amp; Reverb Time</h3><p>Convert tempo and note divisions into milliseconds and hertz.</p><span class="tool-row__io">BPM → ms · Hz</span></a></li>
        <li class="tool-row" data-reveal><a href="/resources/tools/note-frequency/"><h3>Note &amp; Frequency</h3><p>Move between note names, MIDI numbers, frequencies and cents.</p><span class="tool-row__io">Note ⇄ Hz ⇄ MIDI</span></a></li>
        <li class="tool-row" data-reveal><a href="/resources/tools/sample-pitch/"><h3>Sample Pitch &amp; Rate</h3><p>See how transposition changes playback rate, duration and loop tempo.</p><span class="tool-row__io">Semitones → rate · length</span></a></li>
      </ul>
      <p style="margin-top:2rem"><a class="link" href="/resources/tools/">All tools →</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 6 · archive -->
  <section class="band" aria-labelledby="legacy-title">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-head"><h2 id="legacy-title">The archive is context, not borrowed identity</h2><p>Old addresses stay useful where the historic intent can be verified. Former files and authorship are not claimed by the new publisher.</p></div>
      <article class="record" data-reveal><div class="record__grid"><div><span class="flag">Historical resource</span><h3>The Spy Guitar</h3></div><div><p>A documented former Ableton sampler instrument. The current page explains what can be verified and why no unlicensed file is redistributed.</p><dl class="record__facts"><div class="fact"><dt>Rights</dt><dd>Not transferred with the domain</dd></div><div class="fact"><dt>Status</dt><dd><span class="status" data-state="unavailable">Documentation only</span></dd></div></dl><a class="link" href="/legacy/the-spy-guitar/">Read the archive record →</a></div></div></article>
      <article class="record" data-reveal><div class="record__grid"><div><span class="flag">Historical resource</span><h3>Bang My Twister</h3></div><div><p>A former Max for Live/Twister project documented without claiming the previous operator’s work. External records are linked at their source.</p><dl class="record__facts"><div class="fact"><dt>Rights</dt><dd>Remain with their respective owners</dd></div><div class="fact"><dt>Status</dt><dd><span class="status" data-state="external">External records</span></dd></div></dl><a class="link" href="/legacy/bang-my-twister/">Read the archive record →</a></div></div></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 7 · strings and applications -->
  <section class="band band--wide story" aria-labelledby="story-title">
    <div class="shell">
      <figure class="story__media" data-reveal><img src="/assets/story-viola-back.png" width="1376" height="774" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Editorial illustration of a viola and microphone in a quiet room."><figcaption class="kicker" style="margin-top:.75rem">Editorial illustration — not a documented session</figcaption></figure>
      <div class="story__body"><h2 id="story-title">One instrument, three different jobs</h2><div><p>A viola can be a live ceremonial voice, an exposed recording or source material for a playable instrument. The useful workflow changes with the job — and so do timing, microphone, rights and delivery decisions.</p><div class="story__links"><a class="link" href="/recording/">Recording →</a><a class="link" href="/music-for-media/">Music for Media →</a><a class="link" href="/sound-design/">Sound Design →</a></div></div></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 8 · latest -->
  <section class="band band-surface" aria-labelledby="latest-title">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-head"><h2 id="latest-title">Published for the relaunch</h2><p><a class="link" href="/journal/">Open the journal →</a></p></div>
